From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: confirm the retained Uke SDP input budget

The Uke trial acknowledged an input-current SET of zero but a later fresh
GET still reported 500000 uA. Confirm the existing bounded request with a
fresh property-5 GET under the same lock and source generation. Accept a
firmware clamp below the requested ceiling, but reject an exceeded budget.

Return a terminal error after an unconfirmed SET; the DWC3 worker must not
replay an actuator as though this were preflight readiness. Preserve the
500 mA ceiling, both SDP observations and all existing lifecycle/wet guards.
This readback does not qualify electrical USB suspend or battery charge stop.

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1498,6 +1498,19 @@
 	ret = qcom_battmgr_request_property(battmgr, BATTMGR_USB_PROPERTY_SET,
 					  USB_INPUT_CURR_LIMIT, val->intval);
+	if (ret)
+		goto out;
+	/* An ACK alone does not confirm the retained input budget. */
+	ret = qcom_battmgr_request_property(battmgr, BATTMGR_USB_PROPERTY_GET,
+					  USB_INPUT_CURR_LIMIT, 0);
+	if (ret || generation != qcom_battmgr_uke_generation(battmgr) ||
+	    battmgr->usb.current_limit > (unsigned int)val->intval) {
+		dev_info_ratelimited(battmgr->dev,
+			 "SDP budget not confirmed: requested=%d reported=%u uA error=%d\n",
+			 val->intval, battmgr->usb.current_limit, ret);
+		/* Post-SET uncertainty must not enter the worker's readiness retry. */
+		ret = -EREMOTEIO;
+	}
 out:
 	mutex_unlock(&battmgr->lock);
 	return ret;
 }

